Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  08 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 21 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSIES  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 56                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 46 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and no designation as to site  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm aggregate of soft  tan cores of tissue  submitted in toto in cassette A  Gross Description by  Joe Serra Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  Carolyn R Kline  M D  Daniel Benjamin Kopans  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSIES , Positive.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Private Outside MGH MEEI MRN  REMOVED_DATE Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  Resident  Gabrielle Baker  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 78 year old woman with a history of IDC in the right breast diagnosis in  REMOVED_CASE_ID   S P radiation  tamoxifen  now with palpable mass in left breast and abnormal mammogram  BI RADD 5   now undergoing core biopsy  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  A  BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE ADENOCARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Sections of the core biopsy reveal infiltrating nests and cords of malignant epithelial cells with associated desmoplasia  The tumor cells are mostly small with increased nucleus to cytoplasm ratio and eccentrically placed nuclei  In some areas there is a prominent single file pattern suggesting a component of lobular differentiation  An immunohistochemical stain for e cadherin demonstrates focal weak staining in a minority of tumor cells  In the context of the morphologic findings  the immunohistochemical staining pattern suggests a component of lobular carcinoma or a poorly differentiated ductal carcinoma loss of expression of e cadherin  The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and Her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ hybridization studies for Her2 neu gene amplification will be reported in an addendum  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected 